  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry through Friday, then rain associated with\nHurricane Isaias arrives over the weekend.\n\nHigh pressure remains in control through Friday resulting in\nclear skies and above normal temperatures. \n\nHurricane Isaias continues to strengthen in Gulf this morning,\nnow a Category 1 on the Saffir-Simpson scale. It is expected to\ngain forward speed today and then make landfall along the Gulf \nCoast sometimes late Friday. After landfall Isaias will quickly\nweaken and become extra- tropical as it interacts with an upper\nwave that is currently centered over southern Texas. The remnant\ncenter will move north through the lower Mississippi Valley \nregion and ultimately through the Ohio Valley by Sunday.\n\nConfidence continues to increase that a period of areawide rain\nwill fall beginning Saturday, continuing into Sunday. Overall, \nrainfall appears to be beneficial given forecast amounts of 1 to\n2 inches falling over a 48 hour period...therefore flooding \nthreat appears to be low at this time. However, favorable \nsoutheast flow, given the current forecast track, may allow for \nlocalized higher amounts along the eastern slopes of the Blue \nRidge due to upslope enhancement.\n\nWedging high pressure appears to be rather strong, so have\ntrended temperatures down several degrees on Sunday. Have also\ntrimmed out any mention of thunder given the stable airmass that\nis expected to be in place.",
